cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TOAP: The Token-Optimized Agent Protocol"
message: "If you use this software or paper, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sharma
    given-names: Trilochan
    email: parnishklpo@gmail.com
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
repository-code: "https://github.com/parnish007/TOAP"
abstract: >-
  TOAP is a reference-minimized, two-plane protocol for inter-agent messaging in
  multi-agent LLM systems. Shared content is stored once and exchanged by
  reference rather than re-transmitted, with a byte-optimized control plane
  separated from a tokenizer-aligned semantic plane, a broker-mediated context
  store with per-context ACLs and capability-lattice provenance, and a reference
  materialization spectrum. The accompanying paper reports an honest token
  accounting (symbolic opcodes save bytes but few tokens) and a controlled
  multi-model pilot showing that a summarizing baseline can beat reference
  passing on tokens at equal accuracy, so TOAP's value rests on losslessness,
  in-band security, and systematization.
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - large language models
  - agent protocol
  - token efficiency
  - context management
  - prompt injection
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-05-30"
